    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="11[a]">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ger">Ger</ref> 11[a]</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11[a]" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="454" ed="#liebermann"/>[11[a]] on wintra erian ⁊ in miclu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gefyrstu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> timber cleofan,</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#gobbitt" n="26" corresp="#wit-b">On wintra erian 7 in miclum gefyrstum . tim|ber cleofan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="336" ed="#rabin-doml"/>On wintra erian and in miclum gefyrstum timber cleofan,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="454" ed="#liebermann"/>im Winter pflügen und in grossen Frösten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ger_11-a.lnote.de.1"/> Bauholz spalten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ger_11-a.lnote.de.2"/>,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">in winter plough, and in hard frosts split timber,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#gobbitt" corresp="#wit-b">During the winter to plough and during the great frost to cleave timber.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="337" ed="#rabin-doml"/>During the winter, one is to plow, fell trees during the great frost,</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann's 11 is split here into four rows.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">Rabin’s 11 covers the rows 11[a], 11[b], 11[c], 11[d]; it is given here, in the first.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ger_11-a.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">253</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">So Sweet, Kluge</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Thus Sweet, Kluge</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ger_11-a.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">253</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Jede Hufe zu Stoke liefert dem Herrn 4 <hi rend="italic">foðera aclofenas gavolwyda</hi>; Bi 594. Das <hi rend="italic">wudu</hi> nächster Z. ist also Brennholz</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Each hide at Stoke supplies the lord with 4 <hi rend="italic">foðera aclofenas gavolwyda</hi>; Bi 594. The <hi rend="italic">wudu</hi> of the next l. is therefore firewood</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
